From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH] opensbi: K3 suspend P0/P1-activation changes (manifest)

This file previously carried a hand-written summary that was not a
valid git patch (audit finding 1, 2026-11-20). The qualified OpenSBI
source is now pinned as a COMPONENT in sources.lock.json:

  component: opensbi
  revision:  b4152e0761ac1986dfd313876eaff8d7f63cd703
  repository: workdir/k3-maintained-efi/opensbi-controller-trace-diagnostic (local)
  artifact:  fw_dynamic sha256 2f14c5c85bf91e1c... (v21g/v21h hardware-qualified)

The commit contains, relative to the original spacemit K3 opensbi
tree (no surviving clean upstream identity; see the component note):

  P0 batches  explicit suspend-type dispatch; genuine type-0 WFI
              before any vote/mask/IMSIC/cache change; backend error
              propagation with the hart/type/error diagnostic
  v15 fix     dispatch hoist: type validation precedes every
              hardware change (zero CSR/PMU writes on rejection)
  v16 fix     ENOTSUPP-fallback translation: the wrapper fails
              NON_RET_DEFAULT outright so sbi_hsm cannot consume
              ENOTSUPP as a generic-fallback request (the v14/v15
              hart wedges)
  v21         K3_HSM_SUSP_CLUSTER_RET (0x11000000) routed through
              RPMI_HSM_SRV_HART_SUSPEND (k3_rpmi_hsm_route_suspend):
              deny pre-hardware; grant = plain WFI (v21f corruption
              panic fixed: a grant licenses no per-hart vote)

Future OpenSBI changes diff against the pinned commit and ship as
numbered patches in this directory; the component revision advances
with each qualified cycle.

QUIET-DIAGNOSTIC FIX (the LPI-2 lesson, pin 51a9d0f9):

The rpmi-hsm deny print fired from the idle path at cpuidle
retry frequency; five harts printing every denial saturated the
115200-baud console and took the network down (the first LPI-2
flash, 2026-11-21). Rate-limited to ONCE PER HART: the error
code returned to the caller is the durable signal; the console
line is a boot-time aid. This is the transition-path serial
rule applied to the print that predated it.

--- a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c  (addition)
@@ rpmi_hsm_suspend
 	rc = __rpmi_hsm_suspend(type);
+	/* once per hart; further denials are silent */
+	{ static unsigned long reported;
+	  if (!(reported & (1UL << (current_hartid() % 64))) {
+	      reported |= ...;
+	      sbi_printf("rpmi-hsm: hart %u suspend type %#x failed: %d (once; ...)",
+			 current_hartid(), type, rc); } }
